  "problem": "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-x+5y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$=32.$",
